<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cyril Ramaphosa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1952">1952</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Matamela Cyril Ramaphosa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cyril Ramaphosa is a South African politician who has been president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> since 2018. A trade unionist who founded the National Union of Mineworkers, he led the ANC's team in the negotiations that ended apartheid, then became a wealthy businessman. Elected ANC leader in December 2017, he replaced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacob-zuma">Jacob Zuma</a> and in 2024 formed a Government of National Unity after the ANC lost its majority.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cyril-ramaphosa.jpg" alt="Cyril Ramaphosa" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lula Oficial · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cyril_Ramaphosa_in_2026.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
